cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ARES: A Real-fluid Equations Solver"
abstract: >-
  An open-source compressible flow solver for the Euler and Navier-Stokes
  equations on multi-block structured grids, written in modern Fortran, for
  real-fluid flows: thermodynamic and transport properties are interpolated
  from tabulated real-fluid data, and low-Mach preconditioning keeps the
  density-based scheme accurate from nearly incompressible to hypersonic
  regimes. It includes RANS turbulence closures, implicit residual smoothing,
  multigrid, and OpenMP/MPI parallelism.
type: software
